# Step 28, its third pull request's first part: custom commands, the
# interface's third round of review fixes. A command held at an interrupt or
# refused `turn_running` is given back, never sent again; a `/name` typed
# before the session's first `commands/list` answers waits for it, for a
# bound on the application's clock, and goes as a command when the session
# has no list; any `/a:b` goes as a command; and a left-out file's raw name
# is drawn sanitised. Broken one at a time, with the tests that must fail.

[break] a-held-command-is-sent-at-an-interrupt
rule: A custom command among the held prompts at an interrupt comes back into the editor as it was typed: sent, its script would run after the person stopped.
